consent/before-choice          error    consent                                                A tracker that needs consent sent a hit, set a cookie or wrote storage before the visitor chose.
consent/after-reject           error    consent                                                A tracker that needs consent sent a hit, set a cookie or wrote storage after Reject, on the page, a later page or the reload.
consent/after-withdraw         error    consent                                                A tracker that needs consent sent a hit, set a cookie or wrote storage after the visitor withdrew consent (run withdraw).
consent/reject-granted         error    consent                                                After Reject, a Consent Mode update granted ad_storage or analytics_storage, or a Google hit carried gcs G101, G110 or G111.
consent/reject-not-kept        error    consent                                                After Reject, the banner showed again on a later page or the reload, or the CMP's stored choice was gone.
consent/reject-broken          error    consent                                                The Reject button was clicked and didn't take while the CMP's API reject worked, so visitors can't reject (--click button,api).
consent/no-default             error    consent                                                Google tags sent hits with no gcs and no Consent Mode default was ever set.
consent/server-side            error    consent                                                The site's server sent a Meta Conversions API or GA4 Measurement Protocol event for a visitor who rejected or withdrew (--echo).
consent/script-before          error    consent                                                A tracker script, Google Tag Manager included, loaded before the choice or after Reject (--consent-mode strict).
consent/default-late           warning  consent                                                The Consent Mode default was set only after the first Google hit.
consent/v2-signals             warning  consent                                                The Consent Mode default lacks ad_user_data or ad_personalization, or a Google hit's gcd shows them unset.
consent/accept-not-granted     warning  consent                                                After Accept, no Consent Mode update granted anything and Google hits still said denied.
consent/no-first-layer-reject  warning  consent                                                The banner has no Reject on its first layer, so Echo had to open its settings.
consent/no-banner              warning  consent                                                Trackers that need consent fired or set cookies while no banner showed.
consent/gpc-ignored            warning  consent                                                Advertising trackers fired or set cookies for a visitor who sent Global Privacy Control (run gpc).
consent/tcf-mismatch           warning  consent                                                The CMP's TCF consent string granted a purpose after Reject, or granted none after Accept.
consent/embed                  warning  consent                                                An embed such as YouTube, Vimeo without dnt=1 or Google Maps loaded or set cookies before the choice or after Reject.
consent/cookieless-ping        notice   consent                                                Google tags sent cookieless pings before the choice or after Reject (--consent-mode advanced).
consent/meta-no-consent-api    notice   consent                                                Meta Pixel fired before the choice or after Reject and never received fbq('consent', ...).
consent/click-fallback         notice   consent                                                Echo couldn't find the button and made the choice through the CMP's API, so the button itself wasn't tested.
consent/ignore-expired         notice   consent                                                An ignore: entry passed its until date and no longer hides its issue.
